{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i -C 1 'P57A|vacuum-restricted-itp|aristotle.*closeout|closeout' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"386-\n387:scope: autonomous two-lane theorem formalization, terminal-status Codex closeout, safe artifact staging, and resource-bounded Lean verification\n388-applies_to: cwd=source-workspace; reuse_rule=reuse only after checking the live queues, `state.json`, systemd unit, Lean checkout, and Aristotle task state; no acceptance or advancement is implied by this partial rollout\n--\n393-\n394:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, success: two-lane queues and compact manuscript staging verified)\n395-\n--\n399-\n400:## Task 2: diagnose systemd and quarantine-closeout failures\n401-\n--\n403-\n404:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, partial: recovered closeout path; FF15/P37 advancement unverified)\n405-\n--\n417-\n418:- The live runner is `work/aristotle_autopilot/aristotle_autopilot.py`, configured by `work/aristotle_autopilot/autopilot.toml`. It has independent finite-fiber FF15–FF23 and stabilizer-hyperfinite P37–P46 queues, one active Aristotle task per lane, Codex closeout only at terminal status, and advancement only after both machine-readable acceptance and decision fields. [Task 1]\n419-- Upload staging contains the Lean project, the three approved manuscript files, and `AUTONOMY_POLICY.md`; the policy forbids `sorry`, `admit`, axioms, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, and silent weakening. [Task 1]\n420-- The user systemd timer polls every five minutes. For NVM installation, the service and Python resolution need explicit `PATH` and `AUTOPILOT_CODEX_BIN=<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex`; this run verified `codex-cli 0.146.0`. [Task 2]\n421:- Persist closeout metadata in `work/aristotle_autopilot/state.json` before starting Codex. An interrupted closeout without a machine-readable decision halts for review rather than retrying or advancing ambiguously. [Task 2]\n422-\n--\n425-- symptom: systemd reports `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'` and terminal Aristotle jobs never close out -> cause: the NVM executable is outside noninteractive PATH -> fix: set the absolute Codex path in both the service and runner, then verify the service environment. [Task 2]\n426:- symptom: a closeout consumes about 13 GB and clones/builds Mathlib -> cause: `lake build` was run in a stripped downloaded Aristotle quarantine snapshot with no `.lake` -> fix: inspect/quarantine there, copy only the reviewed candidate to the already-built live project, and run all Lean checks only in that live checkout. [Task 2]\n427:- status guard: at rollout end FF15 and P37 were still active. Do not claim candidate acceptance, FF15 integration, or FF16/P38 submission until `state.json`, closeout output/review, and live Lean checks agree. [Task 2]\n428-\n--\n677-- when the user said “we need the theorem… let’s be complete” -> develop the missing topology machinery as a genuine dependency-gated theorem effort; do not package the load-bearing result as an interface/axiom [Task 3]\n678:- when the user approved unattended automation and Telegram notifications -> halt and alert on blocked/failed/partial/unverified closeouts, but keep routine successful progress quiet [Task 3]\n679-\n--\n1907-- A local validator is worth keeping even when the generic helper exists. The useful check bundle here was schema version/type validation, duplicate-ID checks, dangling-edge checks, legal relation-endpoint checks, and `locator.path` existence or anchor audits where locators are present [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3][Task 4]\n1908:- For repo-root graph work, the quickest structural check is `python3 <original-home>/.codex/skills/project-graph-scheme/scripts/project_graph.py validate --graph project_graph.json`; closeout-quality verification then adds `python3 -m json.tool` on the JSON files, `jsonschema.validate(...)` or `jsonschema -i`, and locator audits when nodes point into real files [Task 2][Task 3][Task 4]\n1909-- The `vsn` rollout established a durable repo-governance pattern: put the human maintenance contract in root `AGENTS.md` plus `PROJECT_GRAPH.md`, keep `project_graph.schema.json` as the typed contract, and use `validate_project_graph.py` as the local enforcement point that all agents can rerun [Task 4]\n--\n1918-- symptom: heading/anchor discovery commands fail during graph seeding -> cause: the regex is more complicated than the task requires -> fix: use simpler `rg` patterns when you only need section headings or labels for locator audits [Task 3]\n1919:- symptom: graph closeouts overstate mathematical certainty -> cause: the graph is treated as a proof artifact instead of a provenance/navigation layer -> fix: state explicitly that the graph records the current support status and does not independently re-prove the mathematics [Task 2][Task 3]\n1920-\n--\n1999-\n2000:- rollout_summaries/2026-07-15T13-22-01-YKcF-general_type_ii_stabilizer_criterion_workline.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/07/15/rollout-2026-07-15T15-22-01-019f65f1-0246-7c83-9c24-dd45127a4929.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-15T13:44:33+00:00, thread_id=019f65f1-0246-7c83-9c24-dd45127a4929, same rollout; distinct routing value for compile/verification and conditional-closeout guidance)\n2001-\n--\n2038-- symptom: `technical.tex` fails on the first compile with an undefined macro -> cause: required math macros such as `\\\\cR` were not defined in the draft preamble -> fix: define custom macros before the first compile and rerun immediately on the exact error [Task 2]\n2039:- symptom: first-pass LaTeX warnings look like unresolved problems at closeout -> cause: references only settle after a second pass -> fix: rerun `pdflatex` and report final-state warnings separately from first-pass noise [Task 2]\n2040-- symptom: visual PDF inspection cannot be completed through the sandboxed image viewer -> cause: rendered PNG paths could not be reopened in this environment -> fix: treat `pdfinfo` plus successful PDF generation as the verified fallback and state that visual inspection remained partial [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
