{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'quarantine_root=aristotle_responses/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-205100d0-563e769a-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57a-49mhqqcx_aristotle\ncandidate_path=$quarantine_root/AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean\nsource_path=<original-home>/Projects/current/bound_beating/formalize_itp/Formalization/InfiniteTensorProductHilbert.lean\nwc -l \"$candidate_path\" \"$source_path\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n-- archive summary --\\\\n'\nsed -n '1,240p' \\\"\"'$quarantine_root/ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n-- candidate declarations --\\\\n'\nrg -n '\"'^(namespace|end |structure|class|def |abbrev |theorem |lemma |instance|noncomputable|axiom|opaque|unsafe)'\"' \\\"\"'$candidate_path\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n-- forbidden-token audit --\\\\n'\nrg -n -i 'sorry|admit|axiom|opaque|unsafe|implemented_by|completion|quotient|hilbert' \\\"\"'$candidate_path\" || true\nprintf '\"'\\\\n-- imports --\\\\n'\nsed -n '1,80p' \\\"\"'$candidate_path\"\nprintf '\"'\\\\n-- source wrappers --\\\\n'\nrg -n -i -C 2 'VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms|ITPCompletionAxioms|canonicalVacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms|axiom|sorry|admit|opaque|unsafe' \\\"\"'$source_path\" || true'","aggregated_output":"  382 aristotle_responses/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-205100d0-563e769a-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57a-49mhqqcx_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean\n  779 <original-home>/Projects/current/bound_beating/formalize_itp/Formalization/InfiniteTensorProductHilbert.lean\n 1161 total\n\n-- archive summary --\n# Summary of changes for run 563e769a-0e9b-4395-9895-e03c81c26851\n## P57A — vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core\n\nCreated exactly one new file, `AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean` (no other project file was modified). `lake build AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct` succeeds with no warnings, the file contains no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, or `implemented_by`, and the exported results depend only on `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n\n### Provenance (requested confirmation)\n\nThe packet nominated the external file `bound_beating/formalize_itp/Formalization/InfiniteTensorProductHilbert.lean` as a port source. **That path does not exist in this workspace**, so no code could be copied from it; the module was therefore developed from scratch against this repository's pinned Mathlib. It imports Mathlib only — no external project is imported or referenced in code — and none of the excluded wrappers (`VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms`, `ITPCompletionAxioms`, `canonicalVacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms`) or any analogue appears. **No completed infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is claimed**; the development stops before any quotient or completion, and makes no GNS, spatial von Neumann tensor product, factor-classification, or manuscript-facing state claim. This is category (1), checked infrastructure.\n\n### Contents (all proved)\n\nAssumptions are exactly the generic ones allowed: `[DecidableEq ι]`, `NormedAddCommGroup (E i)` + `InnerProductSpace ℂ (E i)` for each mode, and the unit-vacuum hypothesis `⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫ = 1` where it is needed.\n\n- `VacuumTensor Ω` — elementary tensors equal to `Ω i` outside a finite active set; `kern` — the finite-product kernel over the union of the active sets; `kern_eq_prod_of_subset` — the kernel is computed by the product over any finite mode set containing both active sets (uses the vacuum normalization); `conj_kern`.\n- `ITPSpan Ω` — the algebraic finite span (free complex vector space on elementary tensors); `itpInner` — its sesquilinear extension, with support-independent evaluation lemmas (`itpInner_eq_sum₂`, `itpInner_eq_sum`, `itpInner_single`, `itpInner_eq_finiteMode`).\n- **Finite-mode realization** (`exists_finiteMode_realization`, and its kernel form `exists_finiteMode_realization_kern`): every finite family of mode-vector families, relative to a finite mode set `s`, is realized by vectors in a finite tensor-product Hilbert space whose inner products are exactly the finite mode products `∏_{i∈s} ⟪u a i, u b i⟫`. This rests on a proved per-mode coordinate theorem (`exists_gram_coords`) obtained from an orthonormal basis of the finite-dimensional span.\n- **Positivity on an arbitrary finite linear combination**: `sum_prod_inner_nonneg` and `itpInner_nonneg` (`0 ≤ itpInner x x` in the complex order, so reality is included), with `re_itpInner_nonneg` for the Mathlib core interface.\n- Conjugate symmetry `conj_itpInner_symm`, additivity `itpInner_add_left`, scalar compatibility `itpInner_smul_left`.\n- Exports: `itpCore : PreInnerProductSpace.Core ℂ (ITPSpan Ω)` and the algebraic vacuum `vacuumVector` with `itpInner_vacuumVector : itpInner Ω Ω = 1`.\n- A small concrete instance (`ι = ℕ`, `E i = ℂ`, `Ω i = 1`) is included as a non-degeneracy check.\n\n### Mathlib gaps encountered and how they were closed\n\nThe pinned Mathlib has an inner product space structure on the *binary* tensor product only; there is no inner product on `PiTensorProduct`, and no Schur/Hadamard positive-semidefiniteness theorem. Rather than postulate either, the finite tensor factor is realized concretely as `EuclideanSpace ℂ (∀ i : s, Fin (m i))` built from per-mode orthonormal coordinates, and positivity is derived from that realization as a genuine norm square. This is a proof-route substitution, not a weakening: both required theorems (finite-mode realization, positivity on a general finite linear combination) are explicit proved statements.\n\n### Deviations from the packet text\n\nOne hypothesis was dropped as unnecessary: `itpInner_vacuumVector` holds without the normalization hypothesis, since the vacuum tensor has empty active set. The hypothesis remains where it is genuinely load-bearing (`kern_eq_prod_of_subset`, `itpInner_nonneg`, `itpCore`, `exists_finiteMode_realization_kern`). No hypothesis was added anywhere.\n\nNo forbidden downstream claim is made, and no predecessor package is used: the module is self-contained shared infrastructure, as required by its `Plan alignment` section.\n\n-- candidate declarations --\n54:namespace AristotleCandidates\n55:namespace VacuumRestrictedITP\n64:theorem exists_gram_coords {F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℂ F]\n88:theorem exists_finiteMode_realization {n : Type*} [Fintype n] (s : Finset ι) (u : n → ∀ i, E i) :\n109:theorem sum_prod_inner_nonneg {n : Type*} [Fintype n] (s : Finset ι) (u : n → ∀ i, E i)\n128:structure VacuumTensor (Ω : ∀ i, E i) where\n139:def VacuumTensor.vacuum (Ω : ∀ i, E i) : VacuumTensor Ω :=\n153:noncomputable def kern (v w : VacuumTensor Ω) : ℂ :=\n158:theorem kern_eq_prod_of_subset (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1) {v w : VacuumTensor Ω} {s : Finset ι}\n171:theorem conj_kern (v w : VacuumTensor Ω) : conj (kern w v) = kern v w := by\n179:abbrev ITPSpan (Ω : ∀ i, E i) := VacuumTensor Ω →₀ ℂ\n183:noncomputable def itpInner (x y : ITPSpan Ω) : ℂ :=\n188:theorem itpInner_eq_sum₂ {x y : ITPSpan Ω} {t₁ t₂ : Finset (VacuumTensor Ω)}\n207:theorem itpInner_eq_sum {x y : ITPSpan Ω} {t : Finset (VacuumTensor Ω)}\n220:theorem conj_itpInner_symm (x y : ITPSpan Ω) : conj (itpInner y x) = itpInner x y := by\n234:theorem itpInner_add_left (x y z : ITPSpan Ω) :\n250:theorem itpInner_smul_left (x y : ITPSpan Ω) (r : ℂ) :\n266:theorem itpInner_nonneg (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1) (x : ITPSpan Ω) : 0 ≤ itpInner x x := by\n288:theorem re_itpInner_nonneg (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1) (x : ITPSpan Ω) :\n295:noncomputable def itpCore (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1) :\n309:noncomputable def vacuumVector (Ω : ∀ i, E i) : ITPSpan Ω :=\n316:theorem itpInner_vacuumVector :\n329:theorem exists_finiteMode_realization_kern (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1)\n344:theorem itpInner_eq_finiteMode (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1) {x y : ITPSpan Ω}\n362:def sanityTensor : VacuumTensor (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ)) where\n379:end Sanity\n381:end VacuumRestrictedITP\n382:end AristotleCandidates\n\n-- forbidden-token audit --\n2:P57A — vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core.\n19:  finite-dimensional (finite-mode) tensor-product Hilbert space\n26:**Deliberate boundary.**  The construction stops before the quotient by the\n27:null space and before any completion.  Nothing here asserts the existence of a\n28:completed infinite tensor-product Hilbert space, a tensor-factor GNS theorem,\n29:or a spatial von Neumann tensor product; no axiom, `sorry`, or interface\n33:`bound_beating/formalize_itp/Formalization/InfiniteTensorProductHilbert.lean` as a model to port.\n37:(`VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms`, `ITPCompletionAxioms`,\n38:`canonicalVacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms`) appear here in any form.\n61:/-- Every finite family of vectors in a complex inner-product space admits finitely many\n85:finite mode set `s`, there is a finite tensor-product Hilbert space\n294:elementary tensors.  No quotient and no completion is taken. -/\n328:tensor-product Hilbert space. -/\n\n-- imports --\n/-\nP57A — vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core.\n\n**Context declaration: Infrastructure only.**  This file makes no manuscript\nclaim.  It develops, from scratch and entirely inside this repository, the\n*algebraic* (finite-support) part of the vacuum-restricted infinite tensor\nproduct of a family of complex inner-product spaces:\n\n* `VacuumTensor Ω` — elementary tensors which agree with the reference\n  (\"vacuum\") vector `Ω i` outside a finite set of active modes;\n* `kern` — the finite-product kernel `∏ ⟪v i, w i⟫`, computed over the union of\n  the two active sets;\n* `ITPSpan Ω` — the free complex vector space on elementary tensors (the\n  algebraic finite span);\n* `itpInner` — the sesquilinear extension of `kern` to `ITPSpan Ω`;\n* `exists_finiteMode_realization` — *finite-mode realization*: for any finite\n  family of elementary tensors and any finite mode set `s` containing their\n  active sets, all pairings are realized as inner products in a genuinely\n  finite-dimensional (finite-mode) tensor-product Hilbert space\n  `EuclideanSpace ℂ (∀ i : s, Fin (m i))`;\n* `itpInner_nonneg` — positivity on an arbitrary finite linear combination,\n  together with conjugate symmetry, additivity and scalar compatibility;\n* `itpCore` — the exported `PreInnerProductSpace.Core ℂ (ITPSpan Ω)`;\n* `vacuumVector` — the algebraic vacuum, with `⟪Ω, Ω⟫ = 1`.\n\n**Deliberate boundary.**  The construction stops before the quotient by the\nnull space and before any completion.  Nothing here asserts the existence of a\ncompleted infinite tensor-product Hilbert space, a tensor-factor GNS theorem,\nor a spatial von Neumann tensor product; no axiom, `sorry`, or interface\nwrapper is used.\n\n**Note on provenance.**  The packet nominated the external file\n`bound_beating/formalize_itp/Formalization/InfiniteTensorProductHilbert.lean` as a model to port.\nThat path is not present in this workspace, so nothing could be copied from it; the development\nbelow was written from scratch against this repository's pinned Mathlib and is self-contained.\nNo external project is imported, and none of the excluded wrappers\n(`VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms`, `ITPCompletionAxioms`,\n`canonicalVacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms`) appear here in any form.\n\n**Note on the finite tensor model.**  The pinned Mathlib provides an inner\nproduct space structure on the *binary* tensor product only\n(`Mathlib/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/TensorProduct.lean`); there is no inner\nproduct on `PiTensorProduct`, and no Schur (Hadamard) product theorem for\npositive semidefinite matrices.  The finite-mode realization below therefore\nuses the concrete finite tensor-product model\n`EuclideanSpace ℂ (∀ i : s, Fin (m i)) ≃ ⨂_{i ∈ s} EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin (m i))`,\nobtained from per-mode orthonormal coordinates.  This is a proved statement,\nnot an assumption, and it is exactly what positivity requires.\n-/\nimport Mathlib\n\nopen scoped ComplexConjugate ComplexOrder InnerProductSpace\n\nnamespace AristotleCandidates\nnamespace VacuumRestrictedITP\n\nuniverse u v\n\n/-! ## Finite Gram coordinates in a single mode -/\n\n/-- Every finite family of vectors in a complex inner-product space admits finitely many\ncoordinates reproducing its Gram matrix: this is the coordinate form of the fact that the\nfamily spans a finite-dimensional subspace, which carries an orthonormal basis. -/\ntheorem exists_gram_coords {F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℂ F]\n    {n : Type*} [Fintype n] (u : n → F) :\n    ∃ (m : ℕ) (lam : n → Fin m → ℂ), ∀ a b, ⟪u a, u b⟫_ℂ = ∑ k, conj (lam a k) * lam b k := by\n  classical\n  set W := Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range u) with hW\n  haveI : FiniteDimensional ℂ W := FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite ℂ (Set.finite_range u)\n  set b := stdOrthonormalBasis ℂ W with hb\n  have hmem : ∀ a, u a ∈ W := fun a => Submodule.subset_span ⟨a, rfl⟩\n  refine ⟨Module.finrank ℂ W, fun a k => ⟪b k, (⟨u a, hmem a⟩ : W)⟫_ℂ, ?_⟩\n  intro a c\n  have h := b.sum_inner_mul_inner (⟨u a, hmem a⟩ : W) (⟨u c, hmem c⟩ : W)\n  have hco : ⟪u a, u c⟫_ℂ = ⟪(⟨u a, hmem a⟩ : W), (⟨u c, hmem c⟩ : W)⟫_ℂ := rfl\n  rw [hco, ← h]\n  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ => by rw [inner_conj_symm]\n\nvariable {ι : Type u} {E : ι → Type v}\n  [∀ i, NormedAddCommGroup (E i)] [∀ i, InnerProductSpace ℂ (E i)]\n\n-- source wrappers --\n120-  simp [hψ i, hφ i]\n121-\n122:/-- Finite products of sectorwise inner products admit a Hilbert-space realization by pure tensors.\n123--/\n124-theorem exists_prod_inner_realization {ι α : Type} [DecidableEq ι]\n--\n441-`algebraicInfiniteTensorInner`, but the missing unconditional theorem is that this kernel is\n442-positive on arbitrary finite linear combinations. This structure packages that missing theorem\n443:along with the sesquilinearity axioms needed by `PreInnerProductSpace.Core`. -/\n444:structure VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms (ι : Type) [DecidableEq ι] (E : ι → Type)\n445-    [∀ i, NormedAddCommGroup (E i)] [∀ i, InnerProductSpace ℂ (E i)] (Ω : ∀ i, E i)\n446-    (hΩ : ∀ i, inner ℂ (Ω i) (Ω i) = 1) where\n--\n468-      (algebraicInfiniteTensorVacuum E Ω) = 1\n469-\n470:namespace VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms\n471-\n472-variable {ι : Type} [DecidableEq ι] {E : ι → Type}\n--\n477-the missing positivity theorem for `algebraicInfiniteTensorInner`. -/\n478-noncomputable def toPreInnerProductSpace\n479:    (h : VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms ι E Ω hΩ) :\n480-    PreInnerProductSpace.Core ℂ (AlgebraicInfiniteTensorProduct ι E Ω) where\n481-  inner := algebraicInfiniteTensorInner E Ω hΩ\n--\n487-/-- The algebraic vacuum-restricted infinite tensor product as an inner product space. -/\n488-noncomputable def toInnerProductSpace\n489:    (h : VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms ι E Ω hΩ) :\n490-    letI : SeminormedAddCommGroup (AlgebraicInfiniteTensorProduct ι E Ω) :=\n491-      h.seminormedAddCommGroup\n--\n497-/-- The completed vacuum-restricted infinite tensor product Hilbert space. -/\n498-noncomputable abbrev ITPCompletion\n499:    (h : VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms ι E Ω hΩ) :\n500-    letI : SeminormedAddCommGroup (AlgebraicInfiniteTensorProduct ι E Ω) :=\n501-      h.seminormedAddCommGroup\n--\n514-completion. -/\n515-noncomputable def toITPCompletion\n516:    (h : VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms ι E Ω hΩ) :\n517-    letI : SeminormedAddCommGroup (AlgebraicInfiniteTensorProduct ι E Ω) :=\n518-      h.seminormedAddCommGroup\n--\n527-/-- The vacuum vector in the completed vacuum-restricted infinite tensor product. -/\n528-noncomputable def ITPCompletionVacuum\n529:    (h : VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms ι E Ω hΩ) :\n530-    letI : SeminormedAddCommGroup (AlgebraicInfiniteTensorProduct ι E Ω) :=\n531-      h.seminormedAddCommGroup\n--\n539-\n540-@[simp] theorem toITP