>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex`, `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'`, quarantine snapshot, `.lake`, `lake build`, state.json\n   409\t\n   410\t## User preferences\n   411\t\n   412\t- when the user said Aristotle may “develop necessary theory” or take “another easier route” -> permit project-local supporting theory and alternative recognizable proofs, but require explicit assumptions and no silent weakening [Task 1]\n   413\t- when the user requested copying only `main.tex` and bibliography -> stage only `manuscript/main.tex`, `manuscript/references.bib`, and `manuscript/mainNotes.bib`, not the whole Overleaf tree [Task 1]\n   414\t- when the user asked to “append the endgame packets and start the loop” -> carry theorem-target packets through the requested endgame rather than stopping at conditional infrastructure interfaces [Task 1]\n   415\t\n   416\t## Reusable knowledge\n   417\t\n   418\t- The live runner is `work/aristotle_autopilot/aristotle_autopilot.py`, configured by `work/aristotle_autopilot/autopilot.toml`. It has independent finite-fiber FF15–FF23 and stabilizer-hyperfinite P37–P46 queues, one active Aristotle task per lane, Codex closeout only at terminal status, and advancement only after both machine-readable acceptance and decision fields. [Task 1]\n   419\t- Upload staging contains the Lean project, the three approved manuscript files, and `AUTONOMY_POLICY.md`; the policy forbids `sorry`, `admit`, axioms, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, and silent weakening. [Task 1]\n   420\t- The user systemd timer polls every five minutes. For NVM installation, the service and Python resolution need explicit `PATH` and `AUTOPILOT_CODEX_BIN=<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex`; this run verified `codex-cli 0.146.0`. [Task 2]\n   421\t- Persist closeout metadata in `work/aristotle_autopilot/state.json` before starting Codex. An interrupted closeout without a machine-readable decision halts for review rather than retryin